THE ☆ MARKER. ja-WP's 各話リスト opens with '話数内の「☆」は、ほぼ全編アニメオリジナルエピソードの回' — an explicit per-episode anime-original marker, and the strongest per-row source this series has (the episode table carries no chapter column). Inside 81-98 it marks 81, 82, 83, 84, 85, 86, 87, 88, 89, 90, 93, 94, 95, 96 and leaves 91, 92, 97, 98 unmarked. 97 and 98 are our two anchored canon rows, which is a clean control: the marker tracks adaptation, not arc grouping.

THE FENCE HOLDS. ep 80 -> ch 32 [31] {31-32 (32 first part)}: shugochara.fandom's Episode 080 infobox reads 'chapter = 31, 32' and ch 31's page lists eps 79/80. ep 97 -> ch 33 [32] {32-33}: the Episode 097 infobox reads 'chapter = 32, 33', ch 32's page lists eps 80 and 97 (both directions), ch 33's lists 97 and 98. Independent corroboration for ep 97 = ch 32's remainder: ch 32's character list is exactly the Tadase flashback cast the episode animates — Betty, Yui Hotori, Mizue Hotori, Tadase's Grandmother, Alto Tsukiyomi, Tsukasa Amakawa — none of whom appear in any episode 81-96. No repair to either fence anchor is needed and none is proposed.

CH 34 IS SPLIT ACROSS EP 91 AND EP 98 (the reason 91/92 are not '☆'). Manga ch 34, in order: the Guardians thank Nobuko Saeki -> she makes Nagihiko admit he was Nadeshiko -> Rima overhears and calls him a liar -> X-eggs on the stairs -> a basketball duel -> Rhythm hatches -> Beat Jumper / Beat Dunk -> Temari re-hatches -> Yamato Maihime -> Queen's Waltz with Rima. The anime pulled ONLY the hatch section forward into ep 91's original basketball story and kept the rest for ep 98 ('復活！輝きの舞姫！' — Saeki's horoscope, Rima's 'I won't hold hands with a liar', Temari's re-hatch, Yamato Maihime), which is already anchored {33-34}. ja-WP states the relocation as a fact in both its なぎひこ and リズム entries. Because the relocated pages sit AHEAD of the anime's own frontier (ch 32 first part) rather than behind it, the 'pages, not numbers' anchor+rearranged shape does not apply here; A44 position-less + graft does.

WHERE THE WRONG TYPES CAME FROM. animefillerlist's live page prints 'manga_canon' on this whole stretch except three rows (its 84/85/86 = our 82/84/85), i.e. it calls the Lulu ?-egg arc manga canon. AFL+AFG count as one source (AFG's type column mirrors it). ja-WP, the licensor synopses and the fandom's chapter fields agree against it 13 rows out of 15.

NOT MY ASK, BUT THE SAME DEFECT CONTINUES BELOW 82: rows 70, 71, 73, 78 and 81 are stored canon while ja-WP marks all five '☆' (81 '潜入！イースター社!?' is a pure Yoru/Kiseki original with no chapter field on the fandom page; 78 'あむちゃんのなが〜い一日!?' likewise sits between the ch-30 and ch-30/31 anchors). Listed in flags, not corrected here.
